hardware.inc is gbdev's Game Boy hardware constant definitions for RGBDS:

  repository: https://github.com/gbdev/hardware.inc
  release:    v6.0.0 (published 2026-10-06, the latest release when fetched)
  file:       https://raw.githubusercontent.com/gbdev/hardware.inc/f8c7a649fe663c4550db6c86a31644852c2dd080/hardware.inc
  commit:     f8c7a649fe663c4550db6c86a31644852c2dd080 (the v6.0.0 tag)
  sha256:     0fdc838feed0911844610ba229912e08f3ddec4a93b1a0a7ae320bd80bc1f4f9
  fetched:    2026-11-07, with curl
  license:    CC0-1.0 (LICENSE, copied from the same commit; sha256
              36ffd9dc085d529a7e60e1276d73ae5a030b020313e6c5408593a6ae2af39673)

It is committed unmodified. `gbcli new` writes it to a new project's
include/hardware.inc (crates/build/src/scaffold.rs embeds it with
include_str!), and crates/build/tests/scaffold.rs checks the embedded bytes
against the sha256 above. To update: fetch a newer release's file and LICENSE
the same way, update this file, and check that `gbcli new` still builds
(the starter uses the v6 names: LCDC_ON, IE_VBLANK, TILEMAP0, OAM_Y_OFS).
